              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda T"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tasty and very moist. The vinegar adds a nice tang to the chicken. I do think it needed a bit more seasoning to it so next time I'll add a little red pepper or something."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MYANGEL6"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tastes almost just like spiedies, but so much easier. Cut the chicken into pieces and wrap in buttered Italian bread for a great taste!",
            "datePublished": "2001-12-22T04:53:18.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "My Hot Southern Mess"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I grew up with this chicken, it was what I always knew as BBQ chicken until I became an adult and having not made it in years I was excited to make this recipe and experiment with the using of mayo in it. Unfortunately, this recipe left me underwhelmed as it was pretty flavorless. With a few tweaks like using apple cider vinegar instead of white vinegar and adding more poultry seasoning may help. Finally, if anyone is curious about the actual recipe, look up it's actual name: Cornell Chicken. Many NY families (especially those with connections to the local fire department, like mine) make their own version of this recipe year round",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-06T03:56:10.008Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
